  SourceId: FznrY4fZASquT6hY
  Slug: sponsored-by-a-stranger
  DisplayName: Sponsored by a Stranger
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/background.svg
  Description: 'You remember the day the stranger approached you to make several
    peculiar inquiries. You don''t remember much about them, other than a large head
    and a frail body. At first, the stranger''s questions seemed odd: how might forgotten
    history nevertheless shape the present, whether an insect hive mind could be
    manipulated at a distance, and so on. You don''t remember all of the questions,
    and you don''t know why you could refuse to answer some but felt compelled to
    answer others. The stranger nevertheless seemed pleased with your responses and
    insisted you would find study at the Magaambya enlightening. You never saw them
    again, but you''re now here at the Magaambya, with more questions than answers
    about your future. Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Intelligence or
    Wisdom , and one is a free attribute boost. You''re trained in your choice of
    the Occultism or Nature skill. You gain your choice of the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Dubious
    Knowledge] or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Quick Identification] skill
    feat. You''re also trained in Insect Lore. Your recommended primary branch is
    the Rain-Scribes.'
  SourceTitle: Pathfinder Strength of Thousands Player's Guide
